1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,527
Most city plans end as a picture.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,836
You can look at it. You can't ask it anything.

3
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:13,303
Agentic City starts somewhere else.

4
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:17,420
Here, the city is a state machine.

5
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:21,280
24.3 square kilometres of Hong Kong's Northern Metropolis:

6
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:25,384
every zone, building, road and pond is machine-readable.

7
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:30,355
Every operation is checked, priced, and can be undone.

8
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:33,540
You say what you want.

9
00:00:33,540 --> 00:00:37,720
The planning agent turns it into a concrete proposal, with a price.

10
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:39,600
Then it stops.

11
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:42,782
Nothing is built until you approve.

12
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:49,802
Approve, and the budget moves, the map changes, and the 3D city follows.

13
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:52,700
Then you measure.

14
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:55,200
One short road, and the average drive to an emergency

15
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:59,488
drops from 4.92 minutes to 3.44.

16
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:05,700
And the finished plan is not a slide.

17
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:08,020
It is two machine-readable files,

18
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:10,400
built to be loaded into an Economic World Model,

19
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:13,440
where households, firms and investors will move in,

20
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:15,849
and live with your decisions.

21
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:23,932
One agent helps you plan the city. The others live in it.

22
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:31,429
Agentic City 2035. A plan you can run.
